From a3302fc5f4c48673433b2093db1f15a3e5d4d217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <x@x>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:49:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Canvas: count wires at junctions; draw text records

Junctions: JunctionGlyph::from_directions counted sides, not wires, so a
node where three wires leave on two sides (right, down, down) became a
Corner without a dot. It now counts wires: three or more always get a
dot (a T when they use exactly three sides), and Corner is only for
exactly two wires at a right angle. A wire that never leaves the point
still counts.

Text records (#35): PageScene draws each Text on its page on a new
Texts layer, at Project::text_position with its anchor, rotation and
height, showing Project::text_string. apply() redraws texts when they
change and when their host symbol, wire or junction (or the host's
device, terminal or potential) changes. A symbol with a DeviceTag text
no longer draws its implicit tag, so no tag is drawn twice; adding or
removing that text redraws the symbol. Potential labels follow a wire's
potential being set, cleared or renamed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
